{{ project_description }}

Generated application version: {{ version }}. The source template has its own
independent release version.

Use Python {{ python_version }} and install the project with `pip install -e '.[dev]'`.
Run `pytest tests/` before configuring a real broker or a Venus OS device.

The CLI requires the firmware's `dbus`, GLib and `vedbus` dependencies and exits
if they are missing. It registers the D-Bus name after creating the service paths.
Battery voltage, current and derived power remain unknown until telemetry arrives;
power uses the latest voltage and current, including zero values.
For tanks, configure `tank.capacity` in cubic metres (1 m³ = 1000 litres).
MQTT tank capacity and remaining-volume values use the same units.
In temperature mode, MQTT `<topic_prefix>/temperature` updates `/Temperature`;
the corresponding `/set` topic uses the same path. Generic mode keeps
`<topic_prefix>/value` and `<topic_prefix>/unit` mapped to `/Value` and `/Unit`.
Device libraries and hardware acceptance must be supplied and checked separately.
The generated installer is not executed by template rendering or template release tests.

Read [the generated tutorial](docs/tutorial.md) before changing configuration or
installing on Venus OS. It explains MQTT TLS requirements, the native installer,
and the limits of the generic service scaffold.
